<div data-cgap-sector="Ammonia Refrigeration &amp; Cold Storage" data-cgap-term="cold storage"></div><p class="lead">An ammonia refrigeration system puts a toxic gas under pressure in the same building as forklift drivers, dock crews and outside contractors. The people who most need the warning are often the ones who have never been inside the machine room.</p><p>These signs are written for the real parts of a cold storage plant: the machine room door and emergency shutdown, compressors and oil pots, relief valve headers, receivers and king valves, evaporators and defrost, blast cells, freezer docks and the eyewash by the coil wash. They are 8x12 aluminum, which holds up to freezer temperatures and washdown better than plastic signs that turn brittle in the cold.</p><h2>What to post, and where</h2><div class="il-areas"><div class="il-area"><h3>Machine room and ventilation</h3><p>Entry, ventilation and emergency shutdown signs for the room that only trained staff should enter. 84 signs. Typical spot: At pits, trenches and basements below CO2 equipment.</p><ul><li><span data-s="DANGER">DANGER</span><a href="/products/danger-co2-machine-room-pit-sign-8x12-aluminum">CO2 Machine Room Pit</a></li><li><span data-s="CAUTION">CAUTION</span><a href="/products/caution-co2-machinery-room-entry-sign-cgap-c12405-812">CO2 Machinery Room Entry</a></li><li><span data-s="NOTICE">NOTICE</span><a href="/products/notice-machinery-room-wind-sock-sign-cgap-n07490-812">Machinery Room Wind Sock</a></li><li><span data-s="SAFETY FIRST">SAFETY FIRST</span><a href="/products/safety-first-machinery-room-sign-cgap-i01295-812">Machinery Room</a></li></ul></div><div class="il-area"><h3>Compressors and oil pots</h3><p>Rotating equipment, hot discharge piping and oil draining steps. 194 signs. Typical spot: On purger and oil drain.</p><ul><li><span data-s="DANGER">DANGER</span><a href="/products/danger-ammonia-oil-drain-sign-8x12-aluminum">Ammonia Oil Drain</a></li><li><span data-s="WARNING">WARNING</span><a href="/products/warning-defrost-coil-drain-plug-sign-cgap-w10729-812">Defrost Coil Drain Plug</a></li><li><span data-s="CAUTION">CAUTION</span><a href="/products/caution-compressor-head-sign-cgap-c01161-812">Compressor Head</a></li><li><span data-s="NOTICE">NOTICE</span><a href="/products/notice-lpr-oil-pot-sign-cgap-n11397-812">LPR Oil Pot</a></li></ul></div><div class="il-area"><h3>Relief valves and vent headers</h3><p>Where a release would come from and who has to stay clear. 123 signs. Typical spot: At vent termination on roof.</p><ul><li><span data-s="DANGER">DANGER</span><a href="/products/danger-ammonia-relief-vent-sign-8x12-aluminum">Ammonia Relief Vent</a></li><li><span data-s="WARNING">WARNING</span><a href="/products/warning-co2-relief-vent-line-sign-cgap-w01133-812">CO2 Relief Vent Line</a></li><li><span data-s="CAUTION">CAUTION</span><a href="/products/caution-purger-cold-pot-sign-cgap-c09105-812">Purger Cold Pot</a></li><li><span data-s="NOTICE">NOTICE</span><a href="/products/notice-purger-strainer-sign-cgap-n17590-812">Purger Strainer</a></li></ul></div><div class="il-area"><h3>Receivers, vessels and king valves</h3><p>High pressure vessels and the valves that isolate the system. 175 signs. Typical spot: On receiver and king valve.</p><ul><li><span data-s="DANGER">DANGER</span><a href="/products/danger-ammonia-receiver-sign-8x12-aluminum">Ammonia Receiver</a></li><li><span data-s="WARNING">WARNING</span><a href="/products/warning-king-valve-sign-cgap-w15496-812">King Valve</a></li><li><span data-s="CAUTION">CAUTION</span><a href="/products/caution-recirculator-pump-sign-cgap-c05067-812">Recirculator Pump</a></li><li><span data-s="NOTICE">NOTICE</span><a href="/products/notice-surge-drum-level-sign-cgap-n12542-812">Surge Drum Level</a></li></ul></div><div class="il-area"><h3>Evaporators and defrost</h3><p>Fans, coils and defrost cycles in the coolers and freezers. 247 signs. Typical spot: On evaporator unit.</p><ul><li><span data-s="DANGER">DANGER</span><a href="/products/danger-evaporator-fans-sign-8x12-aluminum">Evaporator Fans</a></li><li><span data-s="WARNING">WARNING</span><a href="/products/warning-defrost-drain-heater-sign-cgap-w06729-812">Defrost Drain Heater</a></li><li><span data-s="CAUTION">CAUTION</span><a href="/products/caution-defrost-fog-area-sign-cgap-c11396-812">Defrost Fog Area</a></li><li><span data-s="NOTICE">NOTICE</span><a href="/products/notice-defrost-log-sign-cgap-n14426-812">Defrost Log</a></li></ul></div><div class="il-area"><h3>Leak alarms and detection</h3><p>What everyone in the building does when the ammonia alarm goes off. 52 signs. Typical spot: At CO2 detector heads.</p><ul><li><span data-s="DANGER">DANGER</span><a href="/products/danger-co2-gas-detector-sign-8x12-aluminum">CO2 Gas Detector</a></li><li><span data-s="WARNING">WARNING</span><a href="/products/warning-co2-detector-alarm-sign-cgap-w08335-812">CO2 Detector Alarm</a></li><li><span data-s="CAUTION">CAUTION</span><a href="/products/caution-co2-detector-cable-sign-cgap-c19130-812">CO2 Detector Cable</a></li><li><span data-s="NOTICE">NOTICE</span><a href="/products/notice-defrost-fail-alarm-sign-cgap-n18736-812">Defrost Fail Alarm</a></li></ul></div><div class="il-area"><h3>Freezers, blast cells and docks</h3><p>Cold work areas, freezer doors and loading docks. 278 signs. Typical spot: On the plate freezer frame at loading stations.</p><ul><li><span data-s="DANGER">DANGER</span><a href="/products/danger-plate-freezer-sign-8x12-aluminum">Plate Freezer</a></li><li><span data-s="WARNING">WARNING</span><a href="/products/warning-freezer-conveyor-sign-cgap-w15503-812">Freezer Conveyor</a></li><li><span data-s="CAUTION">CAUTION</span><a href="/products/caution-freezer-ramp-sign-cgap-c09377-812">Freezer Ramp</a></li><li><span data-s="NOTICE">NOTICE</span><a href="/products/notice-freezer-racking-sign-cgap-n22372-812">Freezer Racking</a></li></ul></div><div class="il-area"><h3>Pressure tests, pump out and charging</h3><p>Testing, evacuating and charging the system during service work. 55 signs. Typical spot: At the CO2 charging station.</p><ul><li><span data-s="DANGER">DANGER</span><a href="/products/danger-co2-charging-hose-sign-8x12-aluminum">CO2 Charging Hose</a></li><li><span data-s="WARNING">WARNING</span><a href="/products/warning-charging-valves-sign-cgap-w15486-812">Charging Valves</a></li><li><span data-s="CAUTION">CAUTION</span><a href="/products/caution-co2-charging-cart-sign-cgap-c19004-812">CO2 Charging Cart</a></li><li><span data-s="NOTICE">NOTICE</span><a href="/products/notice-co2-charging-station-sign-cgap-n21495-812">CO2 Charging Station</a></li></ul></div></div><h2>Common questions</h2><div class="il-faq"><details><summary>What signs go on an ammonia machine room door?</summary><p>Most plants post that the room contains ammonia and is for trained staff only, where the emergency shutdown and ventilation switches are, and what to do when the leak alarm sounds. Search &quot;ammonia machine room&quot; in the Sign Finder to see every option by install point.</p></details><details><summary>Will aluminum signs hold up in a freezer or blast cell?</summary><p>Yes. Aluminum does not crack in the cold, and the print stays readable through frost and washdown.</p></details><details><summary>Do you have signs for evaporators, defrost and coil cleaning?</summary><p>Yes, including evaporator fan guards, coil frost, defrost and coil cleaner rinse signs. Search the equipment name to see them.</p></details></div><script type="application/ld+json">{"@context": "https://schema.org", "@type": "FAQPage", "mainEntity": [{"@type": "Question", "name": "What signs go on an ammonia machine room door?", "acceptedAnswer": {"@type": "Answer", "text": "Most plants post that the room contains ammonia and is for trained staff only, where the emergency shutdown and ventilation switches are, and what to do when the leak alarm sounds. Search \"ammonia machine room\" in the Sign Finder to see every option by install point."}}, {"@type": "Question", "name": "Will aluminum signs hold up in a freezer or blast cell?", "acceptedAnswer": {"@type": "Answer", "text": "Yes. Aluminum does not crack in the cold, and the print stays readable through frost and washdown."}}, {"@type": "Question", "name": "Do you have signs for evaporators, defrost and coil cleaning?", "acceptedAnswer": {"@type": "Answer", "text": "Yes, including evaporator fan guards, coil frost, defrost and coil cleaner rinse signs. Search the equipment name to see them."}}]}</script>